{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1786509617,"nonce":"F/CtAZWJtg1eRA8BbuCMMWFnhKA=","title":"**What is wrong.** `.github/workflows/` holds exactly one file, `ci.yml`, with eight jobs — `go-lint`, `go-build`, `go-test`, `contract-dto`, `contract-server`, `ui`, `vocabulary`, `reachability`. **Not one of them builds a container image.** `buildx`, `docker/build-push-action`, `docker push` and `packages: write` appear nowhere in the tree; the string `ghcr.io` appears exactly once in the whole repository, and it is `deploy/helm/oto/values.yaml:43` — the chart's default `image.repository`, `ghcr.io/thulasiram/oto`. `justfile` has no docker, image or release recipe: its only `docker` lines are `docker compose` for the local infra stack (`justfile:42`, `justfile:48`).","message":"**The demonstration.** `helm install oto deploy/helm/oto --set secrets.databaseUrl=…` renders the image reference `ghcr.io/thulasiram/oto:0.1.0` — `templates/_helpers.tpl:63-66` falls back to `.Chart.AppVersion` and `Chart.yaml:14` is `\"0.1.0\"`. Nothing has ever pushed to that path, and `git tag` lists **zero tags**, so the pre-install `oto migrate` Job never produces a completing pod and the API and worker Deployments sit in `ImagePullBackOff`. SPEC acceptance criterion 31 (`docs/design/SPEC.md:3811`): *\"`helm install oto` with a Postgres URL and a Slack token is the entire install.\"* `docs/ORCHESTRATION.md:120-123` already concedes the gap in writing: *\"The criterion is still not fully met: no oto container image is published… no release workflow builds or pushes it, so `helm install` works only against a registry the operator populates themselves.\"*\n\n**Why it matters.** The `Dockerfile` is finished work nobody can consume, and it is the only place a real version number exists. It is multi-stage, builds with `CGO_ENABLED=0 GOOS=linux -trimpath -tags timetzdata`, runs on `gcr.io/distroless/static-debian12:nonroot` as `USER 65532:65532`, and stamps three linker variables — `-X main.Version`, `-X main.Commit`, `-X main.BuildDate` (`Dockerfile:35-42`) — which `cmd/oto/version.go:11-15` declares. Nothing else in the repo passes them: `just build` is a bare `go build -o bin/oto ./cmd/oto` (`justfile:218-219`) and CI's is `go build -trimpath -o bin/oto ./cmd/oto` (`.github/workflows/ci.yml:62`), so the binary CI then runs at `ci.yml:63` answers `oto dev`. \"Which build is this\" — the question `GET /api/v1/version` exists to answer — is unanswerable for every artifact this repository currently produces.\n\nWhat the workflow should be, given what is actually there:\n\n- **Trigger.** `push: tags: ['v[0-9]+.[0-9]+.[0-9]+*']`. There are no existing tags, so nothing is being renamed and the pattern is free to be chosen; a `*` suffix admits `v0.1.0-rc.1` without a second workflow.\n- **Permissions.** `contents: read` plus `packages: write`, and the built-in `GITHUB_TOKEN` — GHCR accepts it for a package under the repository's own owner, so no PAT is needed and none should be added.\n- **Multi-arch is genuinely available.** `linux/amd64` and `linux/arm64` are both reachable: CGO is off, nothing in the build stage is host-specific, and `distroless/static-debian12` publishes both architectures. But the `Dockerfile` does **not** declare `TARGETARCH`, so buildx will emulate the compile under QEMU once per platform. The build stage should become `FROM --platform=$BUILDPLATFORM golang:${GO_VERSION}-alpine AS build` with `ARG TARGETARCH` and `GOARCH=$TARGETARCH` on the `go build`, which cross-compiles instead — the change is three lines and is only correct *because* CGO is off.\n- **Tag strategy, and one coupling that will bite.** Publish the immutable `X.Y.Z` **without the `v`**, because `_helpers.tpl:64` requests `.Chart.AppVersion` verbatim and `Chart.yaml:14` carries no `v` — a workflow that publishes only `v0.1.0` leaves the chart's own default broken. Add the `v`-prefixed alias, the `X.Y` moving tag, and the commit `sha` for incident forensics. **`latest` should not be published at all yet:** `Chart.yaml:42` marks the chart `artifacthub.io/prerelease: \"true\"`, and `values.yaml:44-46` argues against floating tags in the chart's own voice — *\"Pin it in production: a floating tag makes 'which build is this' unanswerable\"*. Publishing a `latest` nothing references, while telling operators not to use one, is a contradiction to skip until 1.0.\n- **Stamp the version.** Pass `--build-arg VERSION=${{ github.ref_name }}`, `COMMIT=${{ github.sha }}`, `BUILD_DATE` to the build. The args already exist (`Dockerfile:22-24`); the workflow is the only thing missing.\n- **Provenance yes, SBOM not yet.** `actions/attest-build-provenance` is one step and `id-token: write`, and it answers \"which commit produced this digest\" — the same incident question as above — without a second toolchain. An SBOM is worth less here: the runtime layer ships no packages and the image is one static Go binary whose module graph `go version -m /usr/local/bin/oto` already reports.\n\n**Where.** `.github/workflows/ci.yml` (the only workflow; jobs at `:21`, `:51`, `:65`, `:90`, `:117`, `:132`, `:176`, `:194`), `Dockerfile:10-12` and `:35-42`, `deploy/helm/oto/values.yaml:39-47`, `deploy/helm/oto/templates/_helpers.tpl:63-66`, `cmd/oto/version.go:9-15` — whose comment still reads *\"see the LDFLAGS in the Makefile\"*, and there is no Makefile: it was removed in favour of `just` (ADR 0021, `README.md:76-79`), so that sentence now points at nothing and the release workflow is what should own those flags. `docs/ORCHESTRATION.md:120-123` is the standing admission.\n\n**Scope.** medium\n\n**Done when.** Pushing tag `v0.1.0` produces `ghcr.io/thulasiram/oto:0.1.0` (plus `v0.1.0`, `0.1`, and the sha) whose `docker manifest inspect` lists both `linux/amd64` and `linux/arm64`; `docker run --rm ghcr.io/thulasiram/oto:0.1.0 version` prints `oto v0.1.0 (commit \u003cthe tagged sha\u003e, built \u003ca real timestamp\u003e, go1.26…)` and not `oto dev`; and `helm install` from `deploy/helm/oto` with no `--set image.*` reaches `Running` instead of `ImagePullBackOff`. `docs/ORCHESTRATION.md:120-123` and the ⚠️ blocks at `README.md:103-105` and `values.yaml:39-42` are corrected in the same change, because a stale disclaimer is the defect class this repository keeps finding.","files":null}]}